      "repair_reason": "- [P1] Needs maintainer security-boundary review because the branch broadens command identity parsing and the paired issue remains open.; Needs attention: The diff changes exec approval parsing and has concrete security-boundary concerns around misclassifying wrapper operands as executables.; Review finding: [P1] Keep flock separators before the lock target — src/infra/dispatch-wrapper-resolution.ts:288-290 - [P1] K... (sha=5ad14d2c05fd92f2862968e79a8f63013ffc596b)",
      "review_summary": "The PR changes dispatch wrapper resolution to skip a `--` token after a `flock` lock target, treat `script -- ...` as command payload, and adds two flock trust-plan regression tests.\n\nPR surface: Source +5, Tests +12. Total +17 across 2 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. for the patch defect: source inspection plus live util-linux `flock` behavior and FreeBSD `script` source show the PR can classify operands as executed commands. I did not run the PR branch itself.",
